---
number: 28
title: Be Silent, Be Silent
author: Fanny J. Crosby
composer: W. H. Doane
sp_category: "2"
topic: Reverence
---

[verse 1]
Be silent, be silent,
A whisper is heard;
Be silent, and listen,
Oh, treasure each word.

[chorus]
Tread softly, tread softly,
(Tread softly here, tread softly here),
The Master is here;
Tread softly, tread softly,
(Tread softly here, tread softly here),
He bids us draw near.

[verse 2]
Be silent, be silent,
For holy this place,
This altar that echoes
The message of grace.

[chorus]
Tread softly, tread softly,
(Tread softly here, tread softly here),
The Master is here;
Tread softly, tread softly,
(Tread softly here, tread softly here),
He bids us draw near.

[verse 3]
Be silent, be silent,
Breathe humbly our prayer;
A foretaste of Eden
This moment we share.

[chorus]
Tread softly, tread softly,
(Tread softly here, tread softly here),
The Master is here;
Tread softly, tread softly,
(Tread softly here, tread softly here),
He bids us draw near.

[verse 4]
Be silent, be silent,
His mercy record;
Be silent, be silent,
And wait on the Lord.

[chorus]
Tread softly, tread softly,
(Tread softly here, tread softly here),
The Master is here;
Tread softly, tread softly,
(Tread softly here, tread softly here),
He bids us draw near.
